invariant: INV-13
file: handshake_post.c
catches: unit
reason: a KeyUpdate reply that ch_read could not send keeps
  unexpected_message, which says the peer sent a message out of order,
  where ch_write names internal_error when the same reply fails there.
  bin/unit fails the reply's send and requires internal_error from
  ch_alert_sent.

--- old
    int rc = handle_key_update(t, body[0]);
    if (rc != CH_OK) {
        *alert = ALERT_INTERNAL_ERROR;
    }
--- new
    int rc = handle_key_update(t, body[0]);
